class.description:
Attach a script that implements [method _generate] to this node. In it, build the level out of scenes (rooms, props, enemies) with [method add_part]. Everything generated is a child without an owner, so it is [b]never saved[/b] in the scene: the script makes it again every time.
[b]In the editor[/b] the script runs when the scene is opened (if the script is a [code]@tool[/code] script and [member generate_in_editor] is on), and the result is there to see. The generated nodes show in the Scene dock in a calm colour, without the rename or delete options, and a click in the 3D view selects the whole generated part (a room, a prop) instead of the generator. Each generated part that comes from a scene has the [b]Open in Editor[/b] button: it opens the scene the part was made from. Edit it like any scene and save: the editor then replaces every copy of it in the generated level (see [member part_reload]), so you edit a room while you see it in the level around it.
[b]In the game[/b] the node is only a container: call [method generate] (or let your script's [code]_ready()[/code] do it).
[codeblock]
@tool
extends ProceduralRoot3D

@export var room: PackedScene
@export var count := 6

func _generate() -> void:
    for i in count:
        add_part(room, Transform3D(Basis(), Vector3(i * 12.0, 0, 0)))
[/codeblock]
Rooms that need a property set by the generator can pass it to [method add_part]; the properties are kept and set again when the part's scene is reloaded.
